<section xid="1" props="page-margin-footer:0.5in; page-margin-header:0.5in">
<p style="Normal" xid="2">Node.Js Brad Crash Course<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="3"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="4"><c></c><image dataid="6e0992ec-792f-11f0-9934-fba26619e04e" xid="6" props="height:3.6090in; width:6.5000in"/><image dataid="51ac0264-7930-11f0-9934-fba26619e04e" xid="10" props="height:3.2764in; width:6.5000in"/></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="11"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="12"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="13"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="14"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="26"><image dataid="2220699c-7992-11f0-8a8d-fba26619e04e" xid="20" props="height:3.4937in; width:6.5000in"/></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="21">Node JS comes with REPL thats is <c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="22">R - Read<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="23">E - Evalute<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="24">P - Print <c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="25">L - Loop (loop backfor next input) <c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="27"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="28"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="29"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="30"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="31"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 1" xid="34">Starting with Node JS in VSCode<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="36"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="37">1. Create package.json file<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="38"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="39">command to create pakcage.json <c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="40"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="41"><c props="font-weight:bold">npm init -y</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="42"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="43"><c props="font-weight:normal">2. Create a entry file</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="44"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="45"><c props="font-weight:normal">can be app.js / server.js / index.js anything. </c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="46"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="47"><c props="font-weight:normal">Make sure same file name provided into the package.json as entry point</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="48"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="104"><c props="font-weight:normal">-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Heading 1" xid="49"><c props="font-weight:bold">common JS modules</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="50"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="51"><c props="font-weight:normal">-Its original module system used in node.js</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="52"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="53"><c props="font-weight:normal">- It allows you to split yout code in to multiple files and use require() / module.exports to share code.</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="54"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="55"><c props="font-weight:normal">example as below:</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="56"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="57"><c props="font-weight:bold">util.js</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="59"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="60"><c props="font-weight:normal">function randomNumber(){</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="61"><c props="font-weight:normal">  return Math.floor( Math.random() * 100 ) + 1;</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="62"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-weight:normal">}</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="63"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="64"><c props="font-weight:normal">function celciusToFehrenheit(celcius){</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="65"><c props="font-weight:normal">  return ( </c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">celcius * 9 </c><c props="font-weight:normal">) / 5 + 32;</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="66"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-weight:normal">}</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="67"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="68"><c props="font-weight:normal">//</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-weight:bold">How to export only one function</c><c props="font-weight:normal"> </c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="69"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="70"><c props="font-weight:normal">module.exports = randomNumber;  // here no parenthesis</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="71"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="72"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="78"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-weight:normal">//</c><c props="font-weight:bold">How to export the multiplr functions</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="73"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="74"><c props="font-weight:normal">module.exports = {</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="75"><c props="font-weight:normal">  randomNumber,</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="77"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">celciusToFehrenheit</c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="76"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-weight:normal">};</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="79"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="80"><c props="font-weight:normal">---------------------------------------------------------------</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="81"><c props="font-weight:normal">How to import the functions </c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="82"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="83"><c props="font-weight:bold">server.js</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="87"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="88"><c props="font-weight:bold">//import one function</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="89"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="95"><c props="font-weight:normal">const </c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">randomNumber = require(‘./util);</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="94"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="96"><c props="font-weight:bold">//Import multiple functions</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="97"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="90"><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal">If util.js exported multiple functions then we must import all multiple functions</c><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="91"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="92"><c props="font-weight:normal">const {</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">randomNumber,celciusToFehrenheit </c><c props="font-weight:normal">} = require(‘./util’);</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="98"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="99"><c props="font-weight:normal">//use the function in server .js</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="100"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="101"><c props="font-weight:normal">console.log(“random Number = “, </c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">randomNumber()</c><c props="font-weight:normal">)</c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">;</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="102"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="103"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">console.log(“ </c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">celciusToFehrenheit = </c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">”, </c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">celciusToFehrenheit(10)</c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">);</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="105"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="106"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Heading 1" xid="107"><c props="lang:en-US">ES Modules  (ECMAScript module)</c><c props="lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="108"><c props="lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="109"><c props="lang:en-US">//require one additional setting that </c><c props="lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="110"><c props="lang:en-US">- Go to the package.json file and mention “type” : “module”</c><c props="lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="113"><c props="lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="114"><c props="lang:en-US">its common import and export </c><c props="lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="115"><c props="lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="116"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">postController.js</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="119"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="120"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">const post = [{id:001, label:"post Number 1”},</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="121"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">{id:002, label:"post Number 2”},</c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="122"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">]</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="117"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="123"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">function postData = () = &gt; post;</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="124"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="125"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">export postData;</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="126"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="127"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="133"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="134"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="135"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="136"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">server.js</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="129"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="130"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">import {postData} from ‘./util’;</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="131"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="137"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">console.log(postData);</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="132"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="138"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="139"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="140"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 1" xid="141"><c props="lang:en-US">HTTP module and Create Server</c><c props="lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="142"><c props="lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="143"><c props="lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="128"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">Creating Server.</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="144"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="145"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">1. import http</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="146"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="147"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">import http from ‘http’;</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="149"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="150"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">2. use createServer() method of http</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="151"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="152"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">const server =  http.createServer((req, res)=&gt;{</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="153"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">})</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="148"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="118"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">3. Create response using the res</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="155"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="158"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">//write response</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="156"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">res.write(“This is response”);</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="159"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="160"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">//mention header</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="161"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">res.writeHead(200,{“Content-Type”:"text/html”})</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="164"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="157"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="111"><c props="lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">//mention end</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="165"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">res.end(“finished data sending!!!”);</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="166"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="168"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">//listen port number</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="169"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">server.listen(4000, ()=&gt;{console.log(“Server statrted at port : 4000”);})</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="170"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="167"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="112"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">Creating Client</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="171"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="172"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">1. import http</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="173"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">import htto from ‘http’;</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="174"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="177"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="175"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">2. create options object for connection</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="176"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="206"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">//data variable to store the response</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="207"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">let data ="”;</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="209"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="178"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">const options = {</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="186" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">    host:'localhost',<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="181" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">    port:5000,<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="182" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">    path:'/',<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="183" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">    method:'GET'<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="180"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">}</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="184"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="185"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">3. call request method to initiate req</c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="187"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="188"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">const req = http.request(option, (res)=&gt;{</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="189"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="190"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">})</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="191"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="192"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">4. Read the chunks on res </c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="193"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="194"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">res.on(“data”, (chunk)=&gt;{</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="195"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">  console.log(chunk);</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="210"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">data += chunk;</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="196"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">})</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="197"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="198"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US">5. End res </c><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="199"><c props="font-weight:bold; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="200"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">res.on(“end” ()=&gt;{</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="204"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">    console.log(“full response”, data);</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="205"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">})</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="229"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="230"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US">----------------------------------------------------------------------------</c><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="211"><c props="font-weight:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="212" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">1 First, what is res in http.request() callback?</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="213" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="214" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">When you make an HTTP request in Node.js using http.request() (client-side code), the callback receives an object named res — this is an http.IncomingMessage object.<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="215" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="216" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">IncomingMessage is a readable stream in Node.js.<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="217" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">That means the data you receive doesn’t arrive all at once — it comes in chunks over time.<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="218" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="219" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">2 Why .on()?</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="220" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="221" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">.on() is the method used to listen for events on streams (and other EventEmitter-based objects).<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="222" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">Here, res can emit several events, like:<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="223" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="224" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">'data' → when a chunk of data arrives.<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="225" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="226" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">'end' → when all data has been received.<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="227" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="228" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">'error' → if something goes wrong.<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="231" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="232" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">3 Why is data chunked?</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="233" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="234" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">HTTP responses are streams — the server sends data as it’s ready, instead of waiting to finish everything first.<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="235" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">This is more memory-efficient, especially for large responses.<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="236" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="237" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="238" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">---------------------------------<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="239" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">npm i - D nodemon<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="240" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="241" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">npm</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c> - node package manager</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="242" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">i</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c> - install</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="244" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">-D</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c> - shorthand for --save-dev. This means install the package as development dependency  only not for production.</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="246" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">nodemon</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c> - package that automatically restart your node.js server whenever save changes in your file. </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="249" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="251" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="252" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">After installing dependencies it will create a big dependencies folder. we need not to copy the folder whenevr we migratethe code. Just copy the code and skip the dependencies folder and just type npm install it will install all dependencies since in json.package file all dependencies already been mentioned </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="253" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="271" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">in order to run the server.js file continuesly and need not to restart the server again. Do the below changes in package.json</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="275" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="276" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">“start”:"nodemon server.js”</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="277" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="278" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">now run the server with below command</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="279" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="280" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">npm start</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="273" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="255" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="256" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p style="Heading 2" xid="257" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">.gitignore</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="254" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="258" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="259" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">if we want any of the folder to be skipped by pushing into git repository then mention that folder name in .gitignore file </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="263" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="264" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">example as below:</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="265" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="266" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">.gitignore</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="267" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="268" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">node_modules  </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="250" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="269" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="270" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">---------------------------------------------</p>
<p style="Heading 2" xid="281" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">Environmental Variable  &amp; .env</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="283" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="284" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">create a variables which will be accessible across teh project and need not to hard code them in project. <br/><br/><c props="font-weight:bold">benefits</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c> - </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="285" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="286" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">1. Security - improved security and avoid exposing the sensitive data.</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="287" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="288" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">2. flexibillity that can run same code in development, testing and production. </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="289" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="290" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">3. Portability - can easily moved the app between servers. </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="291" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 3" xid="293" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">Steps to create <c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="294" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="295" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">1. create .env</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="298" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="299" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">PORT = 5000</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="300" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="301" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">API_KEY = 454212454512</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="302" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="303" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">2. Update the package.json</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="304" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="305" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">“start” : “nodemon --env-file=.env server.js”</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="306" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="307" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">3. update server.js</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="308" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="309" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">const PORT = process.env.PORT;</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="296" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="325" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="326" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="331" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c props="font-weight:bold">------------------------------------</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="327" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 2" xid="328" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">Req object</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="329" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="332" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">on req object we can check for <c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="333" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">req.url <c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="334" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">req.method<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="330" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="297" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">The default values are </c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="335" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="336" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">req.url            === &gt;      /</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="337" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">req.method    ===&gt;     GET</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="338" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="339" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">if use request the page then url change as per the user request </c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="340" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="341" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">use requested page </c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-weight:bold">http://localhost:5000/about</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="342" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="343" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">req.url        ====&gt; /about</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="344" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="348" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">Note : In such kind of situiations express will be useful to create custom request not only the GET method</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="345" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="350" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="351" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">----------------------------------------------------------</c><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="352" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 2" xid="353" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:26pt">Postman</c><c props="font-size:26pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="354" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:26pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="356" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt">Postman is the desktop tool / client which lets you test the APIs.</c><c props="font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="357" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="358" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt">Instead of writing your own frontend or fetch code everytime, you just hit yuor server endpoint directly wth postman</c><c props="font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="359" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="360" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="361" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="355" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt">---------------------------------------------------------------</c><c props="font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Heading 1" xid="362" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">Loading files<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="363" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="365" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold; font-size:12pt">fs  - default version - callback version</c><c props="font-weight:bold; font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="366" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="367" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">fs stands for the file system, its build in </c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c props="font-weight:bold; font-size:12pt">file module</c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"> which allow yuo to interact with your computer file system. </c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="371" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold; font-size:12pt">We can also do synchonous version = import fs from ‘fs’;</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="372" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">1. Initiate the file system</c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="373" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="374" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">const fs = require(“fs”);</c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="375" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"> </c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="368" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c>2. Read files</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="376" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="613" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">callback version:</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="377" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">fs.readFile(“data.txt’,"utf8“,(err, data)=&gt;{<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="378" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  if(err) err;<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="380" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">console.log(data);<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="379" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c>})</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="614" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="615" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">synchronous version:</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="618" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal">const data = fs.readFile(“./data.txt”, “utf-8”);</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="381" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="382" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="383" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">3. write file<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="384" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="385" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">fs.writeFile(“data.txt”,"hello world!”, (err)=&gt;{<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="386" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">if(err) throw err;<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="389" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="390" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">console.log(“File written succesfully”);<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="387" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="388" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c>})</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="391" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="392" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">4. Append file<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="393" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="394" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">fs.appendFile(“data.txt”."\n New Line”,(err)=&gt;{<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="395" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="397" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">if(err) throw err;<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="398" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">console.log(“append succesful”);<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="399" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c>})</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="364" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="401" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="402" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt">5. Delete file </c><c props="font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="403" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="404" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt">fs.unlink(“data.txt”,(err)=&gt;{</c><c props="font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="405" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt">if(err) throw err;</c><c props="font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="407" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt">console.log(“file deleted succesfully”);</c><c props="font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="406" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c props="font-size:12pt">})</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="408" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="409" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt">.................................................................................................</c><c props="font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="411" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="412" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="410" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold; font-size:12pt">fs - promise version</c><c props="font-weight:bold; font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="414" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="413" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">import fs from ‘fs/promises’</c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="415" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="416" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">Here instead of the callback promises used and used try catch block to throw error</c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="418" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="422" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="423" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">//Example of read file with file system promises version</c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="420" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="424" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">function readFile(){</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="421" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">}</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="419" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">fs.readFile()</c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="425" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="426" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="427" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="428" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt">------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</c><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="429" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal; font-size:12pt"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 1" xid="430" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">Path &amp; URL</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="431" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="432" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">both path and URL are core module of Node.js and no need to install. <c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="434" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 3" xid="435" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">Path</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="436" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="437" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">path module help you work across the files and directory path, in a way that operating system works (windows use ‘\’ and linux use ‘/’)<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="438" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="439" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">1. path.basename(p, [ext])</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="440" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="441" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic">It returns the last portion of the path </c><c props="font-style:italic"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="442" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="443" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">path.basename(“/users/ravi/docs/file.txt”);  //file.txt<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="444" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">path.basename("/users/ravi/docs/file.txt”, “.txt”); //file<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="447" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="448" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">2. path.dirname(p)</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="454" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="455" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic">It returns the directory name of the path</c><c props="font-style:italic"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="456" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="457" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">path.dirname(“user/ravi/docs/file.txt”);  // user/ravi/docs<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="445" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="446" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="458" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">3. <c></c><c props="font-weight:bold">path.extname(p)</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="459" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="460" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal">retruns the extension of the file </c><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="461" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="462" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal">path.extname(“</c><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">user/ravi/docs/file.txt</c><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal">”);  //txt</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="463" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="464" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal">4. path.join([...paths]);</c><c props="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="465" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="467" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal">join all given path segments into one normalized path</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="466" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="468" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal">path.join(“user”, “ravi”,"docs”, “file.txt”);  //user/ravi/docs/file.txt</c><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="469" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="470" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal">5.  path.resolve([...paths])</c><c props="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="471" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="472" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal">resolves a sequence of path into absolute path</c><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="473" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="474" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal">path.resolve(“ravi”,"file.txt”) // ravi/file.txt</c><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="475" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="476" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal">6. path.normalize(p)</c><c props="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="477" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="478" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal">normalize the given path(fixes ..., .  and duplicate slashes)</c><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="479" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="480" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal">path.normalize(“user//ravi/docs../file.txt”);  //user/ravi/file.txt</c><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="481" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="482" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal">IMP- above example / removed and since its /docs.. it will go one directory up , Hence the output as above . </c><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="483" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="484" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="485" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal">7. path.parse(p)</c><c props="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="486" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="487" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal">It returns an object with path parts</c><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="488" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:normal; font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="489" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">path.parse("/users/ravi/docs/file.txt");<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="490" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">/*<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="491" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">{<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="492" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  root: '/',<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="493" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  dir: '/users/ravi/docs',<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="494" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  base: 'file.txt',<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="495" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  ext: '.txt',<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="496" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  name: 'file'<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="497" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">}<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="498" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">*/<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="499" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="500" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">8. path.format(obj)</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="501" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="502" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic">Its opposite of parse, takes object as input and provide the path</c><c props="font-style:italic"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="503" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="505" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">path.format({<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="506" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  dir: "/users/ravi/docs",<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="507" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  base: "file.txt"<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="508" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">}); <c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="509" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">// "/users/ravi/docs/file.txt"<c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="510" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="512" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="513" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="514" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="515" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="516" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="517" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">URL </c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="518" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="519" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="504" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">URL module used to work with url. </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="640" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="641" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">console.log(import.meta);</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="642" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="649" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c>output as below:</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="648" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><br/>[Object: null prototype] {</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="643" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  dirname: 'E:\\NodeJS\\client-server-json\\src',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="644" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  filename: 'E:\\NodeJS\\client-server-json\\src\\urlDemo.js',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="645" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  resolve: [Function: resolve],</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="646" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  url: 'file:///E:/NodeJS/client-server-json/src/urlDemo.js'</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="647" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">}</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="520" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="521" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">1. url.parse(“https://example.com:8080/path/name?foo=bar#hash”);</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="522" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="524" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal">create a object of given URL.</c><c props="font-style:italic; font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="565" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="523" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">{</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="525" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  protocol: 'https:',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="526" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  slashes: true,</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="527" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  auth: null,</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="528" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  host: 'example.com:8080',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="529" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  port: '8080',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="530" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  hostname: 'example.com',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="531" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  hash: '#hash',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="532" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  search: '?foo=bar',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="533" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  query: 'foo=bar',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="534" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  pathname: '/path/name',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="535" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  path: '/path/name?foo=bar',</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="536" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  href: 'https://example.com:8080/path/name?foo=bar#hash'</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="537" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">}</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="538" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="539" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="540" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">2.url.format(urlObject)</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="541" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="542" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic">builds URL string from object</c><c props="font-style:italic"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="543" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="544" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">const myUrlObject = {</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="545" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  protocol: "https:",</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="546" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  host: "example.com",</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="547" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  pathname: "/path/name",</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="548" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">  query: { foo: "bar" }</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="549" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">};</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="550" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="551" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">console.log(url.format(myUrlObject));</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="552" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">// → 'https://example.com/path/name?foo=bar'</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="553" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="554" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="555" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">3. url.resolve(from, to)</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="556" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="557" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic">Resolve a target URL relative to the base URL</c><c props="font-style:italic"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="558" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="559" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">console.log(url.resolve("/one/two/three", "four")); </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="560" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">// → '/one/two/four'</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="561" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="562" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">console.log(url.resolve("http://example.com/one", "/two"));</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="563" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">// → 'http://example.com/two'</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="564" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="566" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="567" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">4. url.pathToFileURL</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="568" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="569" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic">convert a local filesystem path  - &gt; file </c><c props="font-style:italic"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="573" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="574" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">console.log(pathToFileURL(“/users/ravi/docs/file.txt”));</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="575" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="576" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">// → file:///users/ravi/docs/file.txt</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="577" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="578" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="579" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">5. url.fileURLToPath(url)</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="580" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="581" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-style:italic">convert the url to path</c><c props="font-style:italic"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="582" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="584" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">console.log(fileURLToPath("file:///users/ravi/docs/file.txt"));</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="585" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">// → /users/ravi/docs/file.txt</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="583" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="586" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="587" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="588" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="589" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">==================================================================</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="590" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="591" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">Create API </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="592" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="593" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">check for tthe url like </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="594" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">req.url ==="api/data” etc</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="595" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="596" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="597" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">=====================================================================</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="598" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 1" xid="599" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">Middleware</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="600" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="601" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">Middle ware is the function which runs between the request and response.</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="602" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="608" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c>It will have acces to both - request and response. </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="603" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="609" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c>It can make changes in req or res</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="605" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="610" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c>Its useful for security , validation etc </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="606" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="619" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 1" xid="620" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">OS module</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="622" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="623" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">The os module in Node.js is a built-in core module that provides information about the operating system where your Node.js app is running.</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="624" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">It helps you get system-related details such as CPU, memory, network interfaces, OS type, etc</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="625" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="627" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"> Common os module methods</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="628" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">Method	Description</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="629" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.type()	Returns OS name (Windows_NT, Linux, Darwin)</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="630" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.platform()	Returns platform (win32, linux, darwin)</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="631" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.arch()	Returns CPU architecture (x64, arm)</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="632" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.release()	Returns OS version</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="633" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.uptime()	Returns system uptime (in seconds)</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="634" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.totalmem()	Total memory (RAM) in bytes</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="635" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.freemem()	Free memory in bytes</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="636" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.cpus()	Returns info about CPUs/cores</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="637" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.networkInterfaces()	Returns network interfaces info</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="638" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.homedir()	Returns home directory of current user</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="639" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">os.userInfo()	Returns info about the logged-in user</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="626" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="621" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="651" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="652" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="653" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="654" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="655" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="656" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"></p>
<p style="Heading 1" xid="607" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">Event Emmiter</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="658" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="659" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">node.js is the event driven, means many of its API uses the events. </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="660" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="661" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">- HTTP server emit events like ‘request’</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="662" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">- A stream emits “data” and “end” </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="663" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="669" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 3" xid="670" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c><c>import and create EventEmitter</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="664" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="671" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">import EventEmitter from ‘events’;</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="672" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="673" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">//create instance</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="674" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="675" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">const myEmitter = new EventEmitter();</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="677" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="679" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">//simple example below</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="689" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="682" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">//register an event listener</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="683" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">myEmitter.on(“greet”,()=&gt;{</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="685" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"> console.log(“Greeting”);</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="686" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c>})</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="687" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="688" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">myEmitter.emit(“greet”);</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="680" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="690" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">***********************************</p>
<p style="Normal" xid="691" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr">on above example </p>
<p style="Normal" xid="692" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="693" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">.on - </c><c props="font-weight:normal">this is a method provided by EventEmitter to listen for the event</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="709" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="712" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; lang:en-US"></c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">.once -  </c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">its one time listener</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="710" props="margin-top:0.0000in; margin-left:0.0000in; text-indent:0.0000in; dom-dir:ltr; margin-bottom:0.0000in; line-height:1.000000; text-align:left; margin-right:0.0000in"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="711" props="margin-top:0.0000in; margin-left:0.0000in; text-indent:0.0000in; dom-dir:ltr; margin-bottom:0.0000in; line-height:1.000000; text-align:left; margin-right:0.0000in"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; lang:en-US; text-position:normal; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; text-decoration:none">.off - </c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; lang:en-US; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; text-decoration:none">removing listener</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="694" props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; dom-dir:ltr; color:000000; lang:en-US; text-align:left; text-position:normal; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; text-decoration:none"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="695" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">greet - </c><c props="font-weight:normal"> this is event name</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="696" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="697" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:bold">()=&gt;   - </c><c props="font-weight:normal">Event handler function, that runs when event emitted.</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="702" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="703" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; text-decoration:none; color:000000; font-size:12pt; text-position:normal; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">myEmitter.emit(“greet”) - </c><c props="font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:12pt; color:000000; text-decoration:none; text-position:normal; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; lang:en-US">emitter emits the custom event</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="700" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="701" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="698" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="699" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-weight:normal"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="681" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="678" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Heading 2" xid="676" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="list-tag:1004"></c>Process Objects</p>
<p style="Contents 3" xid="665" props="text-align:left; text-indent:0in; dom-dir:ltr; margin-left:0pt"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="715" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c>in node.js </c><c props="font-weight:bold">process</c><c> object is a global objectthat gives you information and control overthe current node.js process. </c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="716" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="717" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c>We dont need to import them since its built in.</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="718" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="719" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c></c></p>
</section>
